[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-9]   [LINK: (/mænˈhætən, mən-/) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English]   [LINK: (ⓘ) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:En-NYC-Manhattan.ogg]   [LINK: (man-HAT-ən, mən-) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:Pronunciation_respelling_key]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-147]  Mean monthly maxima and minima (i.e. the expected highest and lowest temperature readings at any point during the year or given month) calculated based on data at said location from 1991 to 2020.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-149]  Official weather observations for Central Park were conducted at the Arsenal at Fifth Avenue and 64th Street from 1869 to 1919, and at Belvedere Castle since 1919. [LINK: ([145]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_note-148]

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-322]  The presidential election results for the years 1876–1912 are not strictly comparable with the earlier and later ones because New York County included the  [LINK: (West Bronx) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/West_Bronx]  after 1874 and all of what is now the Borough of  [LINK: (the Bronx) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bronx]  (Bronx County, New York) from 1895 until The Bronx became a separate borough in 1914.


