[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-28]  Freeman, Jess. "Milan's Via Montenapoleone Tops Ranking Of World's Most Expensive Retail Destinations For First Time",  [LINK: (Cushman & Wakefield) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cushman_%26_Wakefield] , November 21, 2024. Accessed December 4, 2024. "Milan's Via Montenapoleone, where rents have risen by nearly a third in the past two years, has overtaken New York's Upper 5th Avenue to be crowned the world's most expensive retail destination, according to Cushman & Wakefield (NYSE: CWK).... Synonymous with fashion and luxury, Via Montenapoleone has steadily climbed the rankings in recent years, reaching second for the first time in 2023. Rents rose 11% to US$2,047 per square foot (psf) in the past 12 months, whereas rents on Upper 5th Avenue (US$2,000) remained flat for a second consecutive year."

