[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-69]  Rybczynski, Witold. "Olmsted's Triumph" Archived December 26, 2015, at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine] ,  [LINK: (Smithsonian (magazine)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smithsonian_(magazine)] , July 2003. Accessed November 20, 2016. "By 1876, landscape designer Frederick Law Olmsted and architect Calvert Vaux had transformed the swampy, treeless 50 blocks between Harlem and midtown Manhattan into the first landscaped park in the United States."

