[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-144]  "Keeping New York City 'Cool' Is The Job Of NASA's 'Heat Seekers'" Archived October 1, 2019, at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine] ,  [LINK: (NASA) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NASA] , January 30, 2006. Accessed November 20, 2016. "The urban heat island occurrence is particularly pronounced during summer heat waves and at night when wind speeds are low and sea breezes are light. During these times, New York City's air temperatures can rise 7.2 °F (4.0 °C) higher than in surrounding areas."

