[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-155]  Sternbergh, Adam. "Soho. Nolita. Dumbo. NoMad? Branding the last unnamed neighborhood in Manhattan." Archived March 25, 2015, at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine] ,  [LINK: (New York (magazine)) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York_(magazine)] , April 11, 2010. Accessed November 20, 2016.

[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan#cite_ref-156]  Pitts, David. "U.S. Postage Stamp Honors Harlem's Langston Hughes" Archived February 2, 2017, at the  [LINK: (Wayback Machine) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wayback_Machine] ,  [LINK: (United States Department of State) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States_Department_of_State] . Accessed November 20, 2016. "Harlem, or Nieuw Haarlem, as it was originally named, was established by the Dutch in 1658 after they took control from Native Americans. They named it after Haarlem, a city in the Netherlands."

