[LINK: (Burns, Ric) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ric_Burns] , and  [LINK: (Sanders, James) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/James_Sanders_(architect)] . New York: An Illustrated History (2003), book version of 17-hour Burns  [LINK: (PBS) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PBS]  documentary,  [LINK: (New York: A Documentary Film) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/New_York:_A_Documentary_Film]

[LINK: (Burrows, Edwin G.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edwin_G._Burrows]  and  [LINK: (Wallace, Mike) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mike_Wallace_(historian)]  (1999).  [LINK: (Gotham: A History of New York City to 1898) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gotham:_A_History_of_New_York_City_to_1898] . New York:  [LINK: (Oxford University Press) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxford_University_Press] .  [LINK: (ISBN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)]   [LINK: (0-195-11634-8) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-195-11634-8] ., The standard scholarly history, 1390pp

Ellis, Edward Robb. The Epic of New York City: A Narrative History (2004) 640pp; Excerpt and text search; Popular history concentrating on violent events & scandals

Homberger, Eric. The Historical Atlas of New York City: A Visual Celebration of 400 Years of New York City's History (2005)

[LINK: (Jackson, Kenneth T.) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kenneth_T._Jackson] , ed. (2010).  [LINK: (The Encyclopedia of New York City) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Encyclopedia_of_New_York_City]  (2nd ed.). New Haven:  [LINK: (Yale University Press) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yale_University_Press] .  [LINK: (ISBN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)]   [LINK: (978-0-300-11465-2) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-300-11465-2] .

Kouwenhoven, John Atlee. The Columbia Historical Portrait of New York: An Essay in Graphic History. (1953)

Lankevich, George J. New York City: A Short History (2002)

McCully, Betsy. City at the Water's Edge: A Natural History of New York (2005), environmental history excerpt and text search

Reitano, Joanne. The Restless City: A Short History of New York from Colonial Times to the Present (2010), Popular history with focus on politics and riots excerpt and text search

[LINK: (Filler, Martin) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Martin_Filler]  (April 2015). New York: Conspicuous Construction. Analysis of architectural and social aspects of "ultra-luxury towers ... the smokestack-like protuberances that now disrupt the skyline of midtown Manhattan."  [LINK: (The New York Review of Books) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Review_of_Books]

Story, Louise and Saul, Stephanie (February 2015). Towers of Secrecy. A series of 6 articles "examining people behind shell companies buying high-end real estate" in midtown Manhattan. Part 1: Time Warner Center: Symbol of the Boom, Part 2: The Mysterious Malaysian Financier, Part 3: The Besieged Indian Builder, Part 4: The Mexican Power Brokers, Part 5: The Russian Minister and Friends, Summary: The Hidden Money Buying Up New York Real Estate.  [LINK: (The New York Times) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_New_York_Times]


